Gavin wrote:
> (37" diagonally, 1920x1080 pixels).

Well, DPI wasn't ever the issue anyway, what is of
interest is that, inside a screen window, you have
room for a 23w*42h character, and still leave room
for the window frame decorations. That's 966 pixels
to be painted per character, which may or may not
have some performance issues for stuff like
explosions and tracking missile weapons across the
screen. I know my 1280x800 monitor has some update
artifacts due to the sheer number of pixels that
need to be repainted at once playing NetHack, and at
over 2GHz CPU rate, that's a bit astounding.

Still, you're probably far better off to choose one
of the GUI versions of NetHack, and play it in ASCII
mode. Very likely they all, already render from
TrueType(tm) or OpenType(tm) fonts anyway, and you
should get some nice kind of result.

For example, the GUI version of NetHack for
MS-Windows that downloads from nethack.org, has a
menu item Map => Fit to Screen that you'd probably
like a _lot_, it does beautiful walls, it uses text
as big as will fit in the play area, and it plays in
its own window, no xterm or similar emulation
required (of course, I'm stuck on MS-Windows, if
you're looking for a Linux solution this may or may
not apply).

HTH

xanthian.

I'd also recommend trying tiles using one of the
Absurd Tile sets, which come in sizes up to
128x128 pixels per tile. They are sheerly gorgeous,
and great when trying to lure spouses or friends
into the NetHack fold.



